# NIFTY QUANT — local secrets (COPY to `.env` and fill in; `.env` is Git-ignored)
#
#   cp .env.example .env        # Windows: copy .env.example .env
#
# Never commit `.env`. Never paste the token into a chat, an issue or a log.
# The engine reads it from the environment and prints only a mask.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstox Analytics Token (read-only, free, valid one year)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Create it at: Upstox Developer API -> Analytics Token
# (https://upstox.com/developer/api-documentation/analytics-token/)
# It can read market data and open the market-data WebSocket; it CANNOT place,
# modify or cancel orders, and it needs no static IP for the market-data APIs.
# One active Analytics Token per account, so replacing it invalidates the old one.
UPSTOX_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=your_upstox_analytics_token_here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: consent record for staging recorded data in the ingestion foundation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Exchange data delivered through a broker API is licensed for personal,
# non-commercial research. The ingestion gate refuses to stage anything without a
# written consent record, so put your own attestation here (or pass
# --consent-record on the command line).
# MARKET_DATA_CONSENT_RECORD=I attest that this data is used for private, non-commercial research only.
